  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1054 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nConfidence is growing that we will enjoy a frontal passage late\nTuesday or Tuesday evening that will allow drier, cooler air to \nspread into the mid state. This would bring an end to the threat \nof excessive heat, and also suppress rain chances for the \nremainder of the week. Near normal temperatures are likely to last\nthrough next weekend, while rain and storm chances look to \nincrease by next weekend as a low pressure system tracks along the\nGulf Coast and spreads deeper moisture into Middle Tennessee.",
